      "message": "feat(fidelity): vouch for a mesh of unknown fidelity (VouchModelFidelity)\n\nA model of a project saved before v59 loads \"fidelity unknown\" and the\ngate refuses its operations until a re-import (#1056). A model whose\nsource file is gone, or whose mesh is exact, could never post again.\n\nVouchModelFidelity { model, by } clears the unknown mark of one model\nand of the stocks copied straight from it, as one labelled undo step\nthat names who vouched. Undo puts each mark back. It refuses by name a\nrecorded coarse chord (#864), an incomplete mesh (#1610), a model that\nis not marked, a name that is not a model and an empty name.\n\nThe record (schema::FidelityVouched { by, rev }) speaks only while the\nmodel has the revision it was given for and no fidelity flag, and rides\nthe project file as the optional key fidelity_vouched (no version step).\n\nMCP tool vouch_model_fidelity (scripts: cam.call), get_job's\nmodels[].fidelity_vouched, and the model page's \"Vouch for this mesh\"\nrow beside the \"Fidelity unknown\" line.\n\nFixes #1339\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
